  "criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "print the object: every code, every month, all three anchors",
      "detail": "3 anchors x 6 codes x 12 months printed whole into the record, no month summarised away.",
      "kind": "instrument",
      "name": "B35-D23-1",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "the September break is tongue-specific, so the code's contents are unchanged and the anchors keep pricing one thing",
      "detail": "It is not. On the China leg in the same months: tongues x9.69 in volume with unit value 3.384 -> 1.552; skins **cold start**, zero for eight months then 1,446,963 kg a month; head meat **dies**, 2,889,986 -> 725,750 kg a month. Feet and offal-nesoi stay flat (x1.44 and x1.54).",
      "kind": "own_reading",
      "name": "B35-D23-2",
      "passed": false
    },
    {
      "criterion": "the other two anchors, same code, same split, do not move: a US-side reclassification would hit every leg at once",
      "detail": "JAPAN: unit value 3.179 -> 3.387 (x1.065), volume x0.68; MEXICO: unit value 2.368 -> 2.260 (x0.954), volume x1.17. So this is a China-leg event, not a code revision.",
      "kind": "known_answer",
      "name": "B35-D23-3",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "the mixture decomposition names what the new flow prices like, and the quantity is matched against what left another code",
      "detail": "if the old flow continued at its own pre-break rate, the implied new flow is 10,741,500 kg at **$1.341/kg**. Head meat on the same leg priced $1.219 before the break, 10.0 per cent away, and it lost 8,656,944 kg over the same four months against the 10,741,500 kg tongues gained. Price and quantity both line up.",
      "kind": "own_reading",
      "name": "B35-D23-4",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "the rule text was chased and the source classes tried are named",
      "detail": "5 classes: English trade press (hits fell in 2014 and 2025, outside the window); USDA FAS and FSIS (nothing on a September 2022 event); **the industry body's own dated filing, USMEF to USTR, 28 October 2022, which names no 2022 access event for pork offal**; Chinese-language search, which surfaced the plant-reinstatement announcement class; that class's one item, robots-blocked from here. The gate is answered on the data instead. Reading the announcement would confirm the mechanism; it would not change the verdict, which is that the code's contents on this leg changed at the break.",
      "kind": "bookkeeping",
      "name": "B35-D23-5",
      "passed": true
    }
  ],
